+{"id":"cex-k-topology-is-not-uniformizable","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://faculty.etsu.edu/gardnerr/5357/notes/Munkres-31.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. ETSU notes prove the K-topology Hausdorff but not regular, while uniformizable spaces are regular. Their composition gives this conclusion, but no source states it as one proposition; it is standard, not novel. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: The K-topology is the classical Hausdorff nonregular example, and every uniformizable space is regular under the library's convention. Composing those established results gives the standard nonuniformizability counterexample directly.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}

